<p>Corpus Christi Public Adjuster works with property owners in Corpus Christi, Nueces County, and surrounding Coastal Bend communities. We do not keep storefront offices in each town. Instead, we come to the damaged home or building, inspect and document the loss, and manage the claim with your insurer. The weather risk changes a lot across a short drive: a beach house on North Padre Island, a brick home in Calallen, and a metal building near Robstown can all face very different claims after the same storm.</p>
<p>To see what has actually been reported near you, search a city or ZIP code with our <a href="/storm-lookup/">storm lookup tool</a> or browse <a href="/storm-history/">Coastal Bend storm history</a>, both built on the NOAA National Centers for Environmental Information (NCEI) Storm Events Database.</p>

<h2>Corpus Christi neighborhoods</h2>
<p>Most of our work happens inside the City of Corpus Christi. The city adopted the 2021 International Codes with local amendments effective August 1, 2023, and its local design criteria list a 140/150 mph design wind speed and a windborne debris zone. Our <a href="/local-building-codes/">Corpus Christi building codes guide</a> explains how that affects repairs.</p>

<h3>Downtown and the Bayfront</h3>
<p>Downtown properties and the Bayfront sit right on Corpus Christi Bay, so storm tide and wind-driven rain matter as much as wind. During Hurricane Hanna on July 25, 2020, NCEI notes that <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=912741" target="_blank" rel="noopener">surge damaged parts of the Corpus Christi Marina and numerous piers along the bay, and inundated North Beach</a>. Mid-rise condos, offices, and older commercial buildings here often have low-slope roofs, parapet walls, and rooftop equipment that need careful inspection. See our <a href="/services/commercial-property-claims/">commercial property claims</a> page.</p>

<h3>Calallen and Annaville</h3>
<p>On the northwest side near the Nueces River, Calallen and Annaville have taken some of the strongest straight-line winds in the county's records. On January 9, 2011, an NWS survey described <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=282647" target="_blank" rel="noopener">damaging winds from Calallen into Annaville, with metal sheds destroyed and minor to major roof damage</a>. On May 10, 2012, straight-line winds near 80 mph swept the same area. Calallen also flooded during the June 2026 rains, with NCEI reporting water about 4 feet deep near Labonte Park at I-37. <a href="/services/wind-damage-claims/">Wind damage claims</a> and flood questions are both common here.</p>

<h3>Flour Bluff</h3>
<p>Flour Bluff sits between the Laguna Madre and Corpus Christi Bay, next to Naval Air Station Corpus Christi. The NAS weather station measured an <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=1332418" target="_blank" rel="noopener">84 mph thunderstorm gust on May 11, 2026</a>, and Tropical Storm Harold brought fence and tree damage to Flour Bluff on August 22, 2023. Many homes here are slab-on-grade with composition shingle roofs, which can lose tabs or crease without obvious damage from the street.</p>

<h3>North Padre Island</h3>
<p>North Padre Island is part of the City of Corpus Christi but lives with barrier-island exposure: Gulf winds, surge, salt air, and elevated construction. Hurricane Hanna made landfall on Padre Island in July 2020. Read more on our <a href="/service-areas/padre-island-tx/">Padre Island public adjuster</a> page.</p>

<h3>Southside</h3>
<p>The Southside, roughly from Saratoga Boulevard and Yorktown Boulevard toward Oso Creek and the Oso Bay area, is mostly newer subdivisions and shopping centers. NCEI records include <a href="https://www.ncdc.noaa.gov/stormevents/eventdetails.jsp?id=713211" target="_blank" rel="noopener">golf ball size hail near Alameda Street and Airline Road on June 4, 2017</a> and a brief EF0 tornado just south of Yorktown Boulevard on May 15, 2015. <a href="/services/hail-damage-claims/">Corpus Christi hail damage claims</a> and <a href="/services/roof-damage-insurance-claims/">roof claims</a> are frequent requests from this part of town.</p>

