<h2>County insurance notes: TWIA, flood, and CRS</h2>
<p>All four Coastal Bend counties we serve (Nueces, San Patricio, Aransas, and Kleberg) are in the TWIA designated catastrophe area. TWIA covers wind and hail only. It is not flood insurance, and the Texas FAIR Plan may not offer wind and hail coverage for a property that is eligible for TWIA. As a result, many coastal owners carry three policies: a homeowners or commercial policy that excludes wind and hail, a TWIA windstorm policy, and a flood policy. After a hurricane, the question of what wind did versus what water did often decides how much each policy pays. Our <a href="/services/twia-windstorm-claims/">TWIA claim help</a> and <a href="/services/flood-damage-claims/">flood damage claims</a> pages go into more detail.</p>
