<p>CRS classes can change. Confirm your community's current status with <a href="https://www.fema.gov/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FEMA</a> or your flood agent before relying on a premium discount. NFIP coverage generally begins 30 days after purchase, with limited exceptions listed on <a href="https://www.floodsmart.gov/whats-covered" target="_blank" rel="noopener">FloodSmart.gov</a>.</p>
<p>Two more points apply everywhere. For properties built, altered, remodeled, enlarged, or repaired on or after January 1, 1988, TWIA eligibility depends on a windstorm certificate of compliance, so roof replacements and repairs usually need TDI windstorm inspection. And TWIA claims must generally be filed within one year of the date of loss. Use our <a href="/claim-deadline-calculator/">claim deadline calculator</a> as a starting point, and talk with a Texas attorney about any deadline to sue.</p>

<h2>What stays the same wherever you are</h2>
<p>The process is the same in every community: a Free Claim Review, a written contract with fees disclosed before any work begins, a detailed inspection, an itemized estimate, and ongoing communication with your insurer. Texas law caps public adjuster compensation at 10% of the insurance settlement, and you may rescind the contract by written notice within 72 hours of signing. We represent the insured only, and claim checks are made out to you.</p>
<p>Whether you need help with a new loss, a <a href="/services/denied-insurance-claims/">denied insurance claim in Corpus Christi</a>, or an <a href="/services/underpaid-insurance-claims/">underpaid claim</a>, start with a <a href="/free-claim-review/">Free Claim Review</a> or call or text [[phone]]. As a Coastal Bend public adjuster, Corpus Christi Public Adjuster can tell you quickly whether your property falls within our area.</p>
